{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue","id":1430080,"title":"Alternative names for Gangrel, Nosferatu and Ventrue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-27T07:57:35-08:00","id":1430080,"title":"Alternative names for Gangrel, Nosferatu and Ventrue","content":"One of my (very minor) pet peeves with Requiem is how it kept some of the Masquerade Clan names, which can also be confusing for new players. Therefore, I was wondering if there were alternative names that have come up in books for those three Clans. I know of &quot;Nosphoros&quot; in the Nosferatu Clan book, which is a good example, but I've yet to read the other Clan books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T09:38:36-08:00","id":1430089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue#post1430080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my (very minor) pet peeves with Requiem is how it kept some of the Masquerade Clan names, which can also be confusing for new players. Therefore, I was wondering if there were alternative names that have come up in books for those three Clans. I know of &quot;Nosphoros&quot; in the Nosferatu Clan book, which is a good example, but I've yet to read the other Clan books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the Ventrue clanbook seems to attempt to connect their origins with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeneid\" target=\"_blank\">Aeneid</a>, claiming they were ancestor-spirits of the trojan people that watched over the hero and his followers in the wanderings that would eventually lead to the founding of Rome in myth. Based on texts in the book, it might be said these guardians were cursed by Juno (possibly through the strix) for their role in Aeneas' success among other things.<br /> <br /> Based on that, calling them <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lares\" target=\"_blank\">Lares</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Di_Penates\" target=\"_blank\">Penates</a>, after the roman guardian spirits, or something related to these (supposed) trojan roots would make considerable sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-27-2020, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T12:14:33-08:00","id":1430108,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu could be Vermes like in <i>Requiem for Rome</i>. It sounds like a slur, because it was, but they used it themselves and it may have come to lose its perjorative connotation. Bear in mind that similar words to &quot;worm&quot; refer to dragons of a kind, so it doesn't <i>have </i>to be that lowly.<br /> <br /> Carnon is the name of a Gangrel bloodline, but it could work for the clan. The propinqui associated Gangrel with a several cultures, unlike other clans. One of them was Gaul and they could be associated with Cernunnos. The association wouldn't necessarily have to be universal or accurate for the name to catch.<br /> <br /> I like Baaldam's idea for Ventrue. You might consider trying to find a Luwian word for ancestor, but that could be quite difficult and possibly inappropriate for Trojans anyway. Plus there's a possibility that they made it all up, in which case they would be unlikely to know more about Anatolian language and culture than anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T12:37:04-08:00","id":1430114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue?p=1430108#post1430108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu could be Vermes like in <i>Requiem for Rome</i>. It sounds like a slur, because it was, but they used it themselves and it may have come to lose its perjorative connotation. Bear in mind that similar words to &quot;worm&quot; refer to dragons of a kind, so it doesn't <i>have </i>to be that lowly.<br /> <br /> Carnon is the name of a Gangrel bloodline, but it could work for the clan. The propinqui associated Gangrel with a several cultures, unlike other clans. One of them was Gaul and they could be associated with Cernunnos. The association wouldn't necessarily have to be universal or accurate for the name to catch.<br /> <br /> I like Baaldam's idea for Ventrue. You might consider trying to find a Luwian word for ancestor, but that could be quite difficult and possibly inappropriate for Trojans anyway. Plus there's a possibility that they made it all up, in which case they would be unlikely to know more about Anatolian language and culture than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was pretty much due to the fact it could be an utterly fabricated origin that i went with a roman name anyway.<br /> <br /> But then i also like to mess with the idea of clan, the definition changing from era and place, so that a group of &quot;Ventrue&quot; could actually be a mish-mash of Julii, Savage generals of the Legio Mortuum that remade themselves to assume the throne of the proquinpi upon the Senex's fall, trojan ancestors that turned blood-drinkers during Rome's birth pangs, Gorgon &amp; Annunaki that seem to blur the line between either Clan, while being older than both by centuries or millenia.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Nosferatu/Vermes/Xolotl or Mekhet/Grettir/Akhud and who knows what else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-25-2021, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T12:53:29-08:00","id":1430116,"title":"","content":"I'm quite fond of Lords Over the Damned's suggestion that the proper name of the clan is Ven, with some suppositions as to its etymology, and that Ventrue is a later Western European derivation and corruption of the name.<br /> <br /> Gangrel is harder; the immediate suggestion that comes to mind is Ekhidna, but even that seems more mythological and scholarly than the Gangrel would be inclined to identify by, more likely something proposed by scholars from other clans. Among themselves I think they're more likely to have a name of practical origin, something that just means &quot;vampire&quot; from whatever land it originated in where the local Gangrel predominated. Savage and Macabre mentions the <i>strega,</i> which has a nice indirect and unverifiable suggestion of owls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T13:09:02-08:00","id":1430117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue?p=1430089#post1430089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, the Ventrue clanbook seems to attempt to connect their origins with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeneid\" target=\"_blank\">Aeneid</a>, claiming they were ancestor-spirits of the trojan people that watched over the hero and his followers in the wanderings that would eventually lead to the founding of Rome in myth. Based on texts in the book, it might be said these guardians were cursed by Juno (possibly through the strix) for their role in Aeneas' success among other things.<br /> <br /> Based on that, calling them <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lares\" target=\"_blank\">Lares</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Di_Penates\" target=\"_blank\">Penates</a>, after the roman guardian spirits, or something related to these (supposed) trojan roots would make considerable sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I like just Aeneid, since it very much makes them king makers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T13:11:52-08:00","id":1430119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue?p=1430116#post1430116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite fond of Lords Over the Damned's suggestion that the proper name of the clan is Ven, with some suppositions as to its etymology, and that Ventrue is a later Western European derivation and corruption of the name.<br /> <br /> Gangrel is harder; the immediate suggestion that comes to mind is Ekhidna, but even that seems more mythological and scholarly than the Gangrel would be inclined to identify by, more likely something proposed by scholars from other clans. Among themselves I think they're more likely to have a name of practical origin, something that just means &quot;vampire&quot; from whatever land it originated in where the local Gangrel predominated. Savage and Macabre mentions the <i>strega,</i> which has a nice indirect and unverifiable suggestion of owls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought about Echidna as well, but I agree it might be a bit too scholarly for the Gangrel. Strega isn't bad but I do believe it's the Italian word for witch, which might be confusing. I might need to dig into Savage and Macabre for more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T13:13:01-08:00","id":1430120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue?p=1430116#post1430116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite fond of Lords Over the Damned's suggestion that the proper name of the clan is Ven, with some suppositions as to its etymology, and that Ventrue is a later Western European derivation and corruption of the name.<br /> <br /> Gangrel is harder; the immediate suggestion that comes to mind is Ekhidna, but even that seems more mythological and scholarly than the Gangrel would be inclined to identify by, more likely something proposed by scholars from other clans. Among themselves I think they're more likely to have a name of practical origin, something that just means &quot;vampire&quot; from whatever land it originated in where the local Gangrel predominated. Savage and Macabre mentions the <i>strega,</i> which has a nice indirect and unverifiable suggestion of owls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Draugr\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> are some i've been tempted to use at times.<br /> <br /> The Hagbui in particular i used as an excuse to make the &quot;punk biker gang vampire&quot; from Near Dark &amp; Lost Boys something more than &quot;modern gothic vampires&quot; in a Blood Types game with friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T13:59:18-08:00","id":1430128,"title":"","content":"I really like the already mentionned Lares for the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> For the Gangrel ... i think that draugr fits very well except ... its lareqdy the name for the humanity 0 state so its a very messy solution (youd need to find another name for humanity 0 and i have no idea).<br /> <br /> I haven't really had any idea going well for nosferatu, maybe vrykolakas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T15:04:06-08:00","id":1430138,"title":"","content":"It took some finding but we\u2019ve had a similar question although this one seems to be doing better.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150421-alternate-names-for-clans-those-taken-from-masquerade-specifically\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150421-alternate-names-for-clans-those-taken-from-masquerade-specifically\"> Alternate names for clans (those taken from masquerade specifically) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150421-alternate-names-for-clans-those-taken-from-masquerade-specifically\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150421-alternate-names-for-clans-those-taken-from-masquerade-specifically </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Context: So in the game i've just started one of my players expressed the desire to play a king of thieves sort of character. He stated as inspirations for his character Varis from Game of Thrones and the Beggar King in John Wick 2. I really like the concept and okayed it and when asked what clan of vampire he wants his character to belong to he goes for gangrel. Now any concept can fit in any of the clan. The clan chosen just mean that a few themes are gonna be put in highlights more than others. In the case of the gangrel i talk with the player if he is interested in exploring themes of savagery </div> </div> </div><br /> Should have something relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T16:05:42-08:00","id":1430146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue#post1430080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my (very minor) pet peeves with Requiem is how it kept some of the Masquerade Clan names, which can also be confusing for new players. Therefore, I was wondering if there were alternative names that have come up in books for those three Clans. I know of &amp;quot;Nosphoros&amp;quot; in the Nosferatu Clan book, which is a good example, but I've yet to read the other Clan books.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Slavic/Serbian folklore, there are vampires that would turn into black animals with shining eyes that are called Psoglav, ( Psoglavi - plural ) which translates to English literally as dog-headed.<br /> You could use that for the Gangrel...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T16:22:29-08:00","id":1430150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue?p=1430146#post1430146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Slavic/Serbian folklore, there are vampires that would turn into black animals with shining eyes that are called Psoglav, ( Psoglavi - plural ) which translates to English literally as dog-headed.<br /> You could use that for the Gangrel...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty good!!! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T04:53:00-07:00","id":1457633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430080-alternative-names-for-gangrel-nosferatu-and-ventrue?p=1430119#post1430119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought about Echidna as well, but I agree it might be a bit too scholarly for the Gangrel. Strega isn't bad but I do believe it's the Italian word for witch, which might be confusing. I might need to dig into Savage and Macabre for more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lamia &amp; Lilitu are some names for similarly monstrous figures - that also blur the lines between mythic individuals and whole classes/races of creatures, unlike Echidna.<br /> Something that crossed my mind while being brought back to this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-01-2021, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}